# ============ What `vercel deploy` must never upload ============
# The Vercel CLI reads THIS file and not .gitignore: without it, a CLI deploy
# uploads the whole working tree — captures/ and fixtures/private/ included,
# which are raw palm frames and a recording of the user's face and hand. This
# product's promise is that a palm image never leaves the device; the deploy
# path must not be the thing that breaks it.
#
# Rule: every line of .gitignore is repeated here verbatim (test/deploy-gate
# fails otherwise), so a CLI deploy uploads what a git deploy would. Anything
# private that is not git-ignored is added below the mirror.

# ---- mirror of .gitignore ----
node_modules
.next
out
.env*
!.env.example
diff.txt
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
lib/generated/
public/mediapipe/
public/ort/
captures/
scan-sessions/
*.session.zip
diff*.txt
test/eval/out/
fixtures/private/
fixtures/golden/**/raw/
fixtures/golden/**/snapshots/
.cache/
next-env.d.ts
.vercel

# ---- private, and not git-ignored ----
# Stills from the user's scan recording (their face is in frame), kept
# untracked in docs/reference by the user.
docs/reference/scan-video-*
